# CSF's north star: the goal and the ordered milestones toward it. Status is
# typed: a done milestone must name a repository path the generator checks
# exists, and an in_progress one must name evidence. PR and issue numbers refer
# to the source monorepo. README.md renders it between generated-block markers.
north_star correctness {
  goal "End-to-end correctness of a robot software stack, proven relative to stated assumptions and checked against them at runtime. The physical world and the models in it are not proven; the envelope around them is: check before execute, contracts at every io boundary, and runtime monitors with a safe fallback.";
  milestone typed_io in_progress "Every io boundary is a typed capability: a service crosses only what its constructor was granted, and the io tree is sorted by crossing tier. Process launch and PostgreSQL are capabilities today; the move into the tier-sorted io directories is planned." {
    uses io; uses tier; uses capability;
    evidence path "io/ipc/proc"; evidence path "io/ipc/db/csfpg";
    evidence pr 290; evidence pr 301; evidence pr 321; evidence issue 264;
  }
  milestone resolved_tiers planned "Each crossing's tier is resolved from runtime and placement state instead of being declared by hand." {
    uses tier; uses placement; uses runtime;
    evidence issue 264;
  }
  milestone ros_seam in_progress "The low-level controller is reached only through the ros seam, whose contract is proven ROS-side and monitored CSF-side with a safe fallback. The stub that answers every call with a typed not-connected error ships; the transport, proof and monitor are planned." {
    uses ros; uses spine; uses check;
    evidence path "io/net/ros"; evidence pr 299;
    cites keymaera_x; cites veriphy;
  }
  milestone turn_executors in_progress "Turn executors are interchangeable behind one contract while CSF owns the session, its context and its tools. Claude Code and the Copilot CLI run as turn executors under the same session gates, chosen by the recipe; CSF does not yet own the session's context." {
    uses turn_executor; uses session; uses claudecode; uses copilotcli;
    evidence path "io/net/model/claudecode"; evidence path "examples/claudecode"; evidence path "io/net/model/copilotcli"; evidence pr 322;
  }
  milestone compilability in_progress "Every unit of the system climbs the compilability ladder from prose to structured, typed, checked and finally discharged, where a checker discharges a stated proof obligation. csfc checks the declared architecture against its Go source on every change, and its check-generated command states lifetime and cleanup obligations that it does not yet discharge." {
    uses compiler; uses compile; uses contracts;
    evidence path "csf/compiler/architecture"; evidence issue 329;
    cites compcert; cites sel4;
  }
  milestone self_improvement in_progress "The system improves itself through Ouroboros, under gates it may not change: mined evidence proposes each change and every accepted change is an operator-approved pull request. The mining loop runs inside CSF: miners mine every log as it changes, a pre-check decides at no model cost which tickets a fixer can take, fixers run through the harness under a daily budget, the merge train merges what passes the gate, and the compounding rate is measured and shown. The slice dispatcher launches the ready slice graph within measured limits with no orchestrator. Unattended fixer launch waits for sandboxed launch." {
    uses ouroboros; uses miner; uses precheck; uses fixer; uses merge_train; uses compounding_rate; uses slice_dispatcher;
    evidence path "services/ouroboros"; evidence path "services/dispatch"; evidence pr 237;
  }
  milestone typed_documentation in_progress "No hand-written documentation: every claim is typed data in architecture.csf and its prose is generated, this section included." {
    uses compiler; uses compile;
    evidence path "csf/compiler/language/architecture.csf"; evidence path "docs/GLOSSARY.md"; evidence pr 333;
  }
  milestone post_training planned "CSF post-trains its own model on its traces and the corrections its operator accepted, once the harness eval suite can score a post-trained model against the frozen one on the same tickets withheld from training. Until then CSF improves the harness only. Deferred by the operator on 2026-10-05; the question is csf_staging issue 415, prompted by NeoHorse-1." {
    uses ouroboros; uses turn_executor; uses brain;
    cites neohorse_1;
  }
}

